        {
            "key": "mg_faqs",
            "scope": "magazine-design",
            "items": [
                [
                    "What are magazine design services?",
                    "Magazine design services cover the end-to-end design of a publication: cover design, layout design, typography, image treatment, and file preparation for print or digital output. The scope depends on whether you need a single issue or an ongoing production arrangement."
                ],
                [
                    "What is the difference between print and digital magazine design?",
                    "Print magazine design is built around press specifications: bleed, colour profiles, and high-resolution file preparation for the press. Digital magazine design is structured for screen reading: layout, file size, and format are all adapted for how people read on a device rather than a printed page."
                ],
                [
                    "Do you offer custom magazine design or work from templates?",
                    "Both. For new publications, we build a custom magazine design system from scratch: grid, typography, cover format, and section structure all developed around your brand and content. For existing publications, we work within your current templates or refine them where needed."
                ],
                [
                    "How long does it take to design a magazine?",
                    "It depends on page count, content volume, and layout complexity. A delivery timeline is confirmed before work begins so your publishing schedule is not disrupted by design production."
                ],
                [
                    "Can you design both the cover and internal layouts?",
                    "Yes. Our magazine design services cover the full publication - magazine cover design, internal spreads, section openers, and all supporting design elements within each issue."
                ],
                [
                    "What file formats do you deliver?",
                    "Print editions are delivered as press-ready PDFs to your printer&#039;s exact specifications. Digital editions are delivered in screen-optimised formats. InDesign source files are transferred on completion, clearly organised for future edits."
                ],
                [
                    "Do you handle ongoing issues or only one-off projects?",
                    "Both. For regular publications, a retainer arrangement means the same team handles each issue without re-briefing. For one-off projects or backlogs, we work on a per-issue or milestone basis depending on the scope."
                ]
            ]
        }
    ]
